<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Impact of Self-Reported Political News Exposure on Implicit Political Bias</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }
        h1, h2, h3 { color: #2c3e50; }
        h1 { border-bottom: 2px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 10px; }
        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 20px 0; }
        th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px; text-align: left; }
        th { background-color: #f2f2f2; }
        tr:nth-child(even) { background-color: #f9f9f9; }
        .plot-container { text-align: center; margin: 30px 0; }
        .plot-container img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid #ddd; }
        .section { margin-bottom: 40px; }
        .note { background-color: #fff3cd; border-left: 5px solid #ffc107; padding: 10px; margin: 10px 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Impact of Self-Reported Political News Exposure on Implicit Political Bias</h1>
    
    <div class="section">
        <h2>1. Methods</h2>
        <p>This analysis examines the relationship between self-reported political news exposure and implicit political bias (measured by IAT D-scores), moderated by political ideology.</p>
        <p><strong>Primary Model:</strong> Linear regression with interaction term: <code>IAT_D ~ news_exposure_z * political_ideology</code></p>
        <p><strong>Sample Size:</strong> {{ model_summary.shape[0] if not model_summary.empty else 'N/A' }} observations</p>
        <p><strong>Alpha Level:</strong> {{ project_config.get('alpha_level', 0.05) if project_config else '0.05' }}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>2. Primary Model Results</h2>
        {% if not model_summary.empty %}
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Term</th>
                    <th>Coefficient</th>
                    <th>Std Error</th>
                    <th>t-value</th>
                    <th>P-value</th>
                    <th>95% CI Lower</th>
                    <th>95% CI Upper</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in model_summary.iterrows() %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row[1]['term'] }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row[1]['coef']) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row[1]['std_err']) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row[1]['t']) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row[1]['pval']) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row[1]['ci_lower']) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row[1]['ci_upper']) }}</td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {% else %}
        <p class="note">No model results available.</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>3. Interaction Plot</h2>
        <div class="plot-container">
            {% if interaction_plot %}
            <img src="{{ interaction_plot }}" alt="Interaction Plot">
            <p><em>Figure 1: Predicted IAT D-scores across levels of news exposure and political ideology.</em></p>
            {% else %}
            <p class="note">Interaction plot could not be generated.</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>4. Robustness Checks</h2>
        {% if not robustness.empty %}
        <h3>Bootstrap Analysis (n=1000)</h3>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Metric</th>
                    <th>Value</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in robustness.iterrows() %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row[1].get('metric', 'N/A') }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row[1].get('value', 0)) }}</td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        
        <h3>Bootstrap Distribution</h3>
        <div class="plot-container">
            {% if bootstrap_plot %}
            <img src="{{ bootstrap_plot }}" alt="Bootstrap Distribution">
            <p><em>Figure 2: Distribution of bootstrap interaction coefficients.</em></p>
            {% else %}
            <p class="note">Bootstrap plot could not be generated.</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        <h3>Alpha Sensitivity</h3>
        <p>Significance status across different alpha levels (0.01, 0.05, 0.10).</p>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Alpha Level</th>
                    <th>Significant?</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <!-- Assuming alpha sweep data is in robustness or separate, simplified here -->
                <tr><td>0.01</td><td>Check robustness_metrics.csv</td></tr>
                <tr><td>0.05</td><td>Check robustness_metrics.csv</td></tr>
                <tr><td>0.10</td><td>Check robustness_metrics.csv</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {% else %}
        <p class="note">No robustness check results available.</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>5. Power Analysis</h2>
        {% if not power_analysis.empty %}
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Metric</th>
                    <th>Value</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in power_analysis.iterrows() %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row[1].get('metric', 'N/A') }}</td>
                    <td>{{ row[1].get('value', 'N/A') }}</td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {% else %}
        <p class="note">No power analysis results available.</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>6. Binary Model Results</h2>
        <p>Model using median-split ideology (binary) for comparison.</p>
        {% if not binary_model.empty %}
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Term</th>
                    <th>Coefficient</th>
                    <th>P-value</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in binary_model.iterrows() %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row[1]['term'] }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row[1]['coef']) }}</td>
                    <td>{{ "%.4f"|format(row[1]['pval']) }}</td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {% else %}
        <p class="note">No binary model results available.</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>7. Diagnostics</h2>
        {% if not diagnostics.empty %}
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Metric</th>
                    <th>Value</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in diagnostics.iterrows() %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row[1].get('metric', 'N/A') }}</td>
                    <td>{{ row[1].get('value', 'N/A') }}</td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {% else %}
        <p class="note">No diagnostic results available.</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</body>
</html>
